---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = '2026-10-02';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy | Adarsh Sarda"
  description="How this portfolio website handles personal data."
  langPaths={{ en: '/privacy/', de: '/de/datenschutz/' }}
  wide
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span>Legal</span> / Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>A factual account of the limited personal-data processing associated with this static portfolio.</p>
  </div>

  <article class="prose legal-copy">
    <p>Last updated: <time datetime={updated}>2 October 2026</time>.</p>

    <h2>Controller and contact</h2>
    <p>
      The person responsible for this portfolio is Adarsh Sarda. For privacy questions or a request about data you have provided directly, email
      <a href="mailto:adarshsarda29@gmail.com">adarshsarda29@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How this site works</h2>
    <p>
      This is a static portfolio hosted through GitHub Pages. It has no visitor accounts, contact forms, newsletter, payment flow, comments, or site-level analytics. The site code does not intentionally set first-party cookies or include advertising pixels.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and technical logs</h2>
    <p>
      GitHub Pages serves the site. GitHub states that it logs a visitor's IP address for security when a GitHub Pages site is visited. GitHub's handling of data on its service is governed by its own
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">privacy statement</a> and
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages#data-collection" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub Pages data-collection documentation</a>.
    </p>
    <p>No separate visitor database or profiling system is configured in this portfolio's source code.</p>

    <h2>Email and external links</h2>
    <p>
      If you choose to email the address above, your email provider and mine process the information in your message so I can reply. I retain correspondence only as long as needed for that purpose or to meet a legal record-keeping obligation.
    </p>
    <p>Links to services such as GitHub and LinkedIn are external. Their privacy practices apply once you visit them.</p>

    <h2>Legal basis and your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Where the GDPR applies, the limited processing needed to operate the site securely relies on legitimate interests under Article 6(1)(f). Processing an email enquiry may also be necessary to respond to a request or comply with a legal obligation. You may have rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection, portability, and complaint to a data-protection authority. The European Commission explains these rights in its
      <a href="https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-topic/data-protection/information-individuals_en" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">information for individuals</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>This notice will be updated if the site's hosting, data collection, or contact methods materially change.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal-copy {
    max-width: var(--max-reading);
  }
</style>
